            "heading": "Pick dubbing and chenille",
            "heading_size": "h2"
          }
        },
        "text": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "text": "<p>Match fiber to the fly. Fine for small dries, coarse for buggy nymphs, chenille when you want segments without a fat noodle.</p><h3>Natural vs synthetic</h3><p>Natural fur dubbing gives organic, spiky texture and can drink water on nymphs. Synthetic stays consistent in color, can add flash, and holds up when you want a clean, repeatable body.</p><h3>Fine vs coarse</h3><p>Fine dubbing for small dries and neat thoraxes. Coarser blends for nymphs, scuds, and streamers where buggy silhouette matters more than polish.</p><h3>Chenille</h3><p>Use when you want segments and bulk without spinning a fat dubbing noodle. Match diameter to hook size so the body does not look stuffed.</p><h3>UV / ice / sparkle</h3><p>A little goes a long way. Use for flash in the thorax or a hint in the blend, not a glitter bomb unless the pattern calls for it.</p><h3>How much</h3><p>Start with half of what you think you need. Thick noodles hide thread control and kill taper.</p>"
          }
        },
